      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Consider incorporating variables such as crime rates, poverty rates, population density, housing stability, and educational attainment. These factors can provide insights into neighborhood stability, access to resources, and social cohesion. You could also explore census demographics such as age distribution, immigrant populations, and health disparities. Additionally, neighborhood 'character' variables like area quality scores (based on walk-score, commute time, etc.), vehicle registration numbers, and business licensing patterns can offer a more nuanced understanding of local conditions.",
