    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The census demographics and immigrant population stuff is interesting. In some of our target zones, those factors seem to correlate heavily with higher frequency in theft and vandalism claims. \n\nIf we wanted to be even more precise for our machine learning model, would it be statistically sound to include variables that specifically track racial or ethnic density in these micro-neighborhoods? I'm trying to figure out if those demographic shifts themselves act as a proxy for the underlying environmental risks we're trying to model.",
